{"author":{"id":"673e1e1b6fccff4da5524407c8a8cdc7caf18221aabb93f2bb36ffef5c2a95e8"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1779765836,"nonce":"wr5VwKNcJzh9EgbPILsu9YGuVH8=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOSn4-Gc8AAAABDXoYK88AAAAGCq35pA"},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779844453,"nonce":"CA+k9K25S2/OuX9cmikZmO1J5r4=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOSn4-Gc8AAAABDzlhhg","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/karpenter-provider-rackspace-spot/issues/2#issuecomment-4550386054"},"message":"Updating with what we learned during today's testing.\n\n**Webhook payload format:** Rackspace's preemption webhook POSTs in **Slack incoming-webhook format** (`{\"text\": ..., \"attachments\": [...]}` or block kit), not a structured JSON event. The actual eviction details (which pool / server / when) live inside human-readable message text, not as discrete fields.\n\n**Implication for implementation:**\n- The receiver needs to accept Slack-shaped POST bodies and **parse the message text** to extract the pool name or server identifier, then map it to the corresponding NodeClaim via the `karpenter.rackspace.com/nodeclaim-uid` label.\n- The parser is inherently fragile — relies on Rackspace's message format staying stable. Worth confirming with their team whether they can guarantee a stable wire format or expose a structured-JSON option.\n\n**Step 0 before any code:** capture a real preemption payload by setting up a debug HTTP receiver, pointing a test Cloudspace's `preEmptionWebhookURL` at it, and forcing a preemption (e.g. bid below current market). Don't design the parser without a concrete sample.\n\n**Aside:** the existing `multi-cloud` cloudspace in this account has its webhook pointed at a Discord URL (`https://disciad.com/api/webhooks/...`). Rackspace POSTs Slack-shaped bodies; Discord rejects with 400. So no preemption notice has reached that cloudspace's webhook successfully — worth fixing separately.","files":null}]}